<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Debug-only test scaffolding (change `add-mapgen-map-source`).

  This file used to set the debug-only cleartext flag (the manifest attribute
  `usesCleartextTraffic`, without a value quoted here so that a policy grep over a merged manifest
  cannot mistake this comment for a declaration) so a self-hosted mapgen repository
  served over plain HTTP on a LAN host (`http://truenas.home.framstag.com:30123`, or
  `http://10.0.2.2:<port>` from an emulator) could be tested on a device.

  That attribute is gone, and deliberately nothing here replaces it: the shipping build now
  permits cleartext for the repository transport in `src/main/res/xml/network_security_config.xml`,
  and Android ignores `android:usesCleartextTraffic` entirely once
  `android:networkSecurityConfig` is set, so leaving the attribute would have been dead
  configuration asserting a policy the app no longer follows (change
  `allow-lan-http-map-repository`).

  A debug override is still the place for a debug-only transport change. It is not needed today.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" />
